{"parentUuid":"a98d417c-764a-49db-9bf4-30c7e0fdb36b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7a9e71f0-2be5-463c-8920-d4053a51af7c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a TEST HARNESS workspace. Your only job is to hold a long-lived background task alive so a backend bounce can be proven not to interrupt it. Do NOT write code, do NOT modify files, do NOT commit, do NOT merge.\n\nDo exactly this:\n\n1. Start the heartbeat probe as a BACKGROUND task (use your Bash tool with run_in_background set to true, NOT nohup and NOT a detached shell -- it must be a task YOU own so the session tracks it as live async work):\n\n   ./modules/app/agent-repl/bin/async-probe.sh wsprobe /tmp/async-probe-wsprobe.log 1\n\n   It ticks once per second and exits ONLY on SIGTERM. It will never return on its own. That is intentional -- do not kill it, do not wrap it in a timeout, and do not restart it under any circumstances.\n\n2. Report back immediately with: the background task id, the probe's pid, and the first three lines of /tmp/async-probe-wsprobe.log so I can confirm it is genuinely ticking.\n\n3. Then STOP and wait. Do not poll the log in a loop, do not start further work, and do not end the background task. If the probe ever stops on its own, say so loudly -- that is the failure this workspace exists to detect.\n\nIf a later message asks you to check the probe, just read the log and report the last few lines plus whether the pid is still alive."}]},"uuid":"9f91e8f7-9719-4888-b71d-cb174b65845e","timestamp":"2026-08-11T16:58:33.989Z","permissionMode":"auto","promptSource":"sdk","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"${HOME}/.config/doom-worktrees/bounce-continuity-probe-hhj","sessionId":"f840991e-f0e6-492b-8ae1-09e8d48c299e","version":"2.1.227","gitBranch":"bounce-continuity-probe-hhj"}
